r_similarity\": 0.8054986, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9a8a8848a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1278, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:48\", \"token_count\": 583, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"Retrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Limitation\\n\\nThis report does not certify overall license compliance. The parser-license question remains open.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"retrospect report on the third parti licens audit under ciph 40 limit this report doe not certifi overal licens complianc the parser licens question remain open\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a8a8848a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"id\": \"d070d37a6418202b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.36175335253142366, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15637466075917666, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8409703, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9a8a8848a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1278, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:48\", \"token_count\": 583, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-41\\n\\n# Slack Thread: License Parser Swap\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-11\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:16] Evan**: Finished the parser swap the audit flagged — pulled out the problem library and dropped in a replacement. Calling that step done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:18] Diana**: Nice turnaround. I'll fold it into the re-scan.\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:21] Charlie**: Did you check the new one's license closely, or just take the package listing at face value?\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:22] Evan**: Fair question — I should have looked harder before wiring it in.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:54] Charlie**: Following up on this — since the replacement turned out to be AGPL, I'm searching for an Apache or MIT alternative that can do the same parsing.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:56] Diana**: Any candidates yet?\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:58] Charlie**: A couple, but neither one covers everything the old library did. Still unresolved as of today — going to keep looking rather than force a bad fit.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 10:22] Alice**: Let me know as soon as one of those candidates looks viable — don't want this dragging past the rest of the release work.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 41 slack thread licens parser swap channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 11 last activ 2026 08 15 2026 08 11 10 16 evan finish the parser swap the audit flag pull out the problem librari and drop in a replac call that step done 2026 08 11 1018 diana nice turnaround i ll fold it into the re scan 2026 08 11 10 21 charli did you check the new one s licens close or just take the packag list at face valu 2026 08 11 10 22 evan fair question i should have look harder befor wire it in 2026 08 15 09 54 charli follow up on this sinc the replac turn out to be agpl i m search for an apach or mit altern that can do the same pars 2026 08 15 09 56 diana ani candid yet 2026 08 15 09 58 charli a coupl but neither one cover everyth the old librari did still unresolv a of today go to keep look rather than forc a bad fit 2026 08 15 10 22 alic let me know a soon a one of those candid look viabl don t want this drag past the rest of the releas work\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8f4f0468a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"id\": \"2536eeff413cf064\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.35974941171854846, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17032371674078348, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8017427, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8f4f0468a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1186, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:17\", \"token_count\": 352, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-40\\n\\n# Slack Thread: License AGPL Reopen\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:14] Diana**: Reopening the license review. The PDF parser Evan swapped in to clear the earlier audit finding turns out to be AGPL-licensed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 10:01] Alice**: AGPL is a dealbreaker for how we distribute this. Are we sure about the licensing?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 10:03] Diana**: Sure — checked the license file directly. It's not something we can ship under our current distribution model.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 10:31] Charlie**: Is there a non-copyleft alternative that covers the same parsing we need?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 10:33] Alice**: Please look.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:08] Diana**: Looking now. Putting this back in progress until we land on a replacement that passes a clean scan.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 40 slack thread licens agpl reopen channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 12 2026 08 12 09 14 diana reopen the licens review the pdf parser evan swap in to clear the earlier audit find turn out to be agpl licens 2026 08 12 1001 alic agpl is a dealbreak for how we distribut this are we sure about the licens 2026 08 12 1003 diana sure check the licens file direct it s not someth we can ship under our current distribut model 2026 08 12 10 31 charli is there a non copyleft altern that cover the same pars we need 2026 08 12 10 33 alic pleas look 2026 08 12 11 08 diana look now put this back in progress until we land on a replac that pass a clean scan\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92f5d6c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-license-agpl-reopen.md\", \"id\": \"2465ca3c92b0e407\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.35343739991927614, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1538437570275374, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8191559, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-license-agpl-reopen.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92f5d6c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-license-agpl-reopen.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-license-agpl-reopen.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 813, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:30\", \"token_count\": 257, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Original Finding: Ghostscript (AGPLv3)\\n\\nThe initial audit flagged `Ghostscript`, used by the `rasterizer` module for PDF-to-image conversion, as AGPLv3-licensed — on the corporate license blacklist because of its viral copyleft terms for any binary distributed to partner sites.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## First Remediation and Reopen\\n\\nThe team swapped in an alternative PDF parser library to replace the Ghostscript dependency, and that swap was initially marked Completed. On follow-up review, however, the replacement library itself turned out to also be AGPL-licensed — the swap solved the specific Ghostscript dependency but reintroduced the same license category problem one layer down. The task was reopened.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Current Status: Unresolved\\n\\nCharlie is now searching for an Apache 2.0 or MIT-licensed PDF parser alternative that meets the module's rasterization requirements. No suitable replacement has been confirmed yet, so this audit item remains **Active (Reopened)** — not resolved.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Secondary Open Item\\n\\nTesseract OCR itself is Apache 2.0, but the `eng.traineddata` model files were sourced from a community repository and their training-corpus provenance has not been verified as public-domain/CC0. This remains a separate, lower-priority open item pending Evan's trace of the `tessdata_best` provenance.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 origin find ghostscript agplv3 the initi audit flag ghostscript use by the raster modul for pdf to imag convers a agplv3 licens on the corpor licens blacklist becaus of it viral copyleft term for ani binari distribut to partner site sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 first remedi and reopen the team swap in an altern pdf parser librari to replac the ghostscript depend and that swap wa initi mark complet on follow up review howev the replac librari itself turn out to also be agpl licens the swap solv the specif ghostscript depend but reintroduc the same licens categori problem one layer down the task wa reopen sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 current status unresolv charli is now search for an apach 20 or mit licens pdf parser altern that meet the modul s raster requir no suitabl replac ha been confirm yet so this audit item remain activ reopen not resolv sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 secondari open item tesseract ocr itself is apach 20 but the eng traineddata model file were sourc from a communiti repositori and their train corpus proven ha not been verifi a public domain cc0 this remain a separ lower prioriti open item pend evan s trace of the tessdata _ best proven\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9d4f0568a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"id\": \"039b629d788751dd\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3524563108160566, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15631760116579518, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8101133, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9d4f0568a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1689, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:12\", \"token_count\": 582, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-27\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Validation\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:04] Bob**: Ran the handshake validation under nominal latency — two nodes on the local network, dozens of connect attempts back to back. No failures.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:05] Evan**: Any dropped or retried handshakes at all?\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:30] Bob**: None. Every attempt authenticated cleanly on the first try at this latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:32] Diana**: We still need the high-latency case covered before this goes anywhere near the field.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:38] Bob**: Agreed, it's next on the list. First cut of the nominal-latency pass looks solid — leaving it in progress until we cover high latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:41] Diana**: Good.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 09:50] Diana**: Reopening this. Ran the handshake over a simulated high-latency link and it's timing out — never completes the exchange.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:08] Bob**: Timing out, or actively failing? Could just be the round trip budget being too tight.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:09] Diana**: Times out. And it gets worse the slower the link — feels like the handshake is doing more work per round trip than it should.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:18] Bob**: That tracks. The AES-256 pipeline we added on the output path adds per-packet overhead, and on a slow link that pushes the exchange past the timeout window. This depends on the encryption work settling down before we can retest — handshake work stays blocked for now.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 27 slack thread node sync handshak valid channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 08 last activ 2026 09 22 2026 08 08 09 04 bob ran the handshak valid under nomin latenc two node on the local network dozen of connect attempt back to back no failur 2026 08 08 09 05 evan ani drop or retri handshak at all 2026 08 08 09 30 bob none everi attempt authent clean on the first tri at this latenc 2026 08 08 09 32 diana we still need the high latenc case cover befor this go anywher near the field 2026 08 08 09 38 bob agre it s next on the list first cut of the nomin latenc pas look solid leav it in progress until we cover high latenc 2026 08 08 09 41 diana good 2026 09 22 09 50 diana reopen this ran the handshak over a simul high latenc link and it s time out never complet the exchang 2026 09 22 10 08 bob time out or activ fail could just be the round trip budget be too tight 2026 09 22 10 09 diana time out and it get wors the slower the link feel like the handshak is do more work per round trip than it should 2026 09 22 1018 bob that track the ae 256 pipelin we ad on the output path add per packet overhead and on a slow link that push the exchang past the timeout window this depend on the encrypt work settl down befor we can retest handshak work stay block for now\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92703ba8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"id\": \"7c000945298cb210\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3323837878840053, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17817527983429332, \"vector_similarity\": 0.69220364, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92703ba8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1559, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:36\", \"token_count\": 450, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nPre-release gate review: Docker slim/CVE, Windows signing, and upstream high-DPI remain open. Audit-log path still a hold — CLI schema and emitted records don't match.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Alice**: We're in pre-release mode. Gate check first: Docker slim-down and CVE work is still open, Windows signing is still open, and we're still blocked upstream on the high-DPI rendering bug. Those stay on the board. Diana, where are we on the audit-log gate?\\n\\n**Diana**: Still a hold. The CLI path and the log records aren't matching the schema we defined. That undercuts the audit trail as release evidence.\\n\\n**Bob**: I've been wiring audit-log generation into the CLI. The shape coming out still isn't consistent with what the schema expects — I've got another pass queued.\\n\\n**Charlie**: So this isn't a packaging issue — it's schema versus emitted records?\\n\\n**Diana**: Yes. Until those match, I can't clear the audit gate.\\n\\n**Evan**: That stacks on top of the Docker and Windows holds Alice listed. Release isn't opening with any of those unresolved.\\n\\n**Alice**: Correct. Security-gate work stays open — Docker slim-down, Windows signing, and we keep the audit mismatch visible as a release blocker. No one closes those today.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep the audit-log gate red until schema and records match.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari pre releas gate review docker slim cve window sign and upstream high dpi remain open audit log path still a hold cli schema and emit record don t match sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 part